# Tickets API: requests you can run from the editor.
# Visual Studio, Rider and IntelliJ run this file as is; VS Code needs the
# "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client). Start the API first:
#   npm start --workspace apps/api          (port 3000)
#   PORT=3200 npm start --workspace apps/api   (if 3000 is taken; change @base)
#   PowerShell: $env:PORT=3200; npm start --workspace apps/api

@base = http://localhost:3000

### Health (answers "healthy"; the BASELINE test expects "ok")
GET {{base}}/health

### All events with availability (the web app's list)
GET {{base}}/events

### Price for 2 tickets at 10.00 EUR, VAT included
POST {{base}}/price
Content-Type: application/json

{ "unitPriceCents": 1000, "quantity": 2 }

### Price with a promo code (10 % off)
POST {{base}}/price
Content-Type: application/json

{ "unitPriceCents": 1000, "quantity": 2, "promoCode": "EARLY10" }

### Availability: evt-1 is sold out
GET {{base}}/events/evt-1/availability

### Availability: evt-2 still has tickets
GET {{base}}/events/evt-2/availability

### Legacy invoice
POST {{base}}/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Dave", "items": [{ "description": "Ticket", "unitPrice": 50, "qty": 2 }] }

# ─── Waitlist ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Join the waitlist of a sold-out event (201, position 1)
POST {{base}}/events/evt-1/waitlist
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "a@example.com" }

### Join again with the same email (200, same position)
POST {{base}}/events/evt-1/waitlist
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "a@example.com" }

### Second person (201, position 2)
POST {{base}}/events/evt-1/waitlist
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "b@example.com" }

### Event is not sold out (409)
POST {{base}}/events/evt-2/waitlist
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "a@example.com" }

### Invalid email (400)
POST {{base}}/events/evt-1/waitlist
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "not-an-email" }

### Waitlist length
GET {{base}}/events/evt-1/waitlist
